{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## /rebar-debug RCA — Phase 1 complete; disposition: ESCALATE (no code change)\n\n**Proven root cause (runtime-confirmed).** `clarity_check_compute`\n(`src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py:163-169`) computes the verdict as the conjunction\n`score >= threshold and floor.passes`, but the returned dict only carries the score half:\n`{\"score\", \"verdict\", \"threshold\"}`. When `floor.passes` is False (e.g. plain-bullet ACs →\n`evaluate_plan_clarity` returns empty `ac_items` → `PlanClarityFloor.passes` is False,\n`src/rebar/_plan_clarity.py:51-56`) while `score >= threshold`, the tool returns\n`verdict: \"fail\"` with `score >= threshold` and no field naming the structural-floor cause.\nThe floor evidence (`ac_items`, `empty_ac_items`, `sentinel_assignments`, `unchecked_ac_lines`)\nis discarded. `ClarityResultOut` (`src/rebar/_mcp_models.py:162-166`), the `ClarityResult`\nTypedDict (`src/rebar/types.py:239-246`) and `clarity_result.schema.json` have no field to\ncarry a reason.\n\n**Proof (discriminating, runtime).** Drove `clarity_check_compute(\"task\", <desc>, 5)` with a\ndescription that scores at the threshold but has non-checkbox ACs:\n`score=5, threshold=5, floor.passes=False → {'score':5,'verdict':'fail','threshold':5}`,\nexit 1, **no `reason` key** — reproduces the live-MCP observation on\n`ruby-griffinish-goitered`. Control: the same body with `- [ ]` checkbox ACs makes\n`floor.passes=True` and returns `verdict:\"pass\"`. So the fail is driven by the floor half,\nwhich is invisible in the output.\n\n**The verdict itself is correct (working-as-designed).** A plan with plain-bullet ACs has a\ngenuine structural defect; `verdict:\"fail\"` is right. `score >= threshold` is only one input\nto the conjunction, not the verdict. The gap is purely *discoverability*: the caller cannot\nsee that the floor failed or why.\n\n**Legitimacy / classification.** The authoritative documented contract —\n`clarity_result.schema.json` — lists exactly `{score, verdict, threshold, passed}` and has NO\n`reason` field, so the current no-reason output *matches* the documented contract. No cited\ndesign authority scoped a `reason` for the *standalone* `clarity_check` surface: the\nfloor-enforcement work (`inherited-evadable-dachshund` / 9385-4ba8, commit `55f2b8036a85`,\nwhich added the `floor.passes` conjunction) deliberately surfaced the floor reason on the\n**P1 plan-review** surface (\"emit blocking P1 findings\") while keeping\n`clarity_check_compute` on its existing pass/fail `{score, verdict, threshold}` shape. The\ncase for a `reason` here rests on **consistency** with the sibling gates (`check_ac`,\n`quality_check`, and clarity's own read-error branch at `_lib_gates.py:49-52`, all of which\nreturn `reason`) — a usability/parity argument, not a violated contract. Adding a `reason`\nfield therefore *creates* new public output rather than *restoring* broken behavior.\n\n**Why ESCALATE (not auto-landed).** The correct fix (the ticket's own AC1–AC3) adds a new\n`reason` field to a public output **contract/schema/API surface** — `clarity_result.schema.json`,\n`ClarityResultOut` (MCP tool output), and the `ClarityResult` TypedDict — and requires a\n**design decision** on the field's exact semantics and format (how it names the failing half,\nand for the structural floor which defect + line it renders). Under this session's orchestrator\nrules that is an escalation trigger (contract/schema/API surface change + design tradeoff), and\nunder the skill's own \"restoration, not creation\" fix-safety rule, new output with no cited\ndesign authority is a feature/scope decision for a human, not a behavior-preserving bugfix.\n\n**Behavioral origin (context, not a defect attribution).** The score>=threshold-yet-fail case\nwas introduced by commit `55f2b8036a85` (`rebar-ticket: 9385-4ba8-ec93-44c3`, \"Enforce\ndeterministic plan clarity floors\"), which added `floor.passes` to the conjunction. Because\nthat behavior is *correct and intended*, no `caused_by` defect edge is recorded — charging an\nescaped defect to correctly-shipped, intended behavior would corrupt the escape-rate metric.\nThe missing standalone `reason` is best read as unfinished parity relative to the P1 surface\nand the sibling gates, to be dispositioned as scoped work if the design is approved.\n\n**No code changed. No tests changed. No sibling sweep run (no fix landed).** Worktree\n`debug/enharmonic-olm` left in place at `origin/main`; it can be retired.\n\n**Decision needed from a human operator:** approve extending the public `clarity_check`\noutput contract with an additive `reason` field (per AC1–AC3), including its exact semantics\nand rendering format, and whether to bring the standalone surface to parity with the P1\nfindings / sibling `reason` gates. If approved, this becomes a scoped implementation\n(the ACs already sketch it) rather than a /rebar-debug auto-fix."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787938085980314001,"uuid":"58e2cdb9-a5c3-49f5-ae41-e3bf88742dee"}